    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "Any of the sulfonylureas can cause hypoglycemia\nwhich can produce shock-like symptoms. Metformin\nand the α-glycosidase inhibitors such as acarbose\nrarely cause ypoglycemia. Glucagon would raise\nplasma glucose.",
