    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "Buspirone is a partial serotonin 5-HT1A-receptor\nagonist that has efficacy comparable to that of\nbenzodiazepines for the treatment of anxiety, but is\nsignificantly less sedating. Alprazolam is an\nintermediate-acting benzodiazepine used in the\ntreatment of generalized anxiety disorder (GAD) but\nstill has some sedation, which would be undesirable\nin this situation. Triazolam is a short-acting\nbenzodiazepine, and trazodone is a heterocyclic\nantidepressant, both used to induce sleep.\nThiopental is a barbiturate sometimes used to\ninduce anesthesia.",
