    "id": "superexam-pharmacology-0053",
    "subject": "pharmacology",
    "originalNumber": 53,
    "stem": "Ampicillin is eliminated by first-order kinetics. Which\nof the following statements best describes the\nprocess by which the plasma concentration of this\ndrug declines?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "There is only 1 metabolic path for drug elimination"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "The half-life is the same regardless of the plasma\nconcentration"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "The drug is largely metabolized in the liver after\noral administration and has low bioavailability"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "The rate of elimination is proportional to the rate\nof administration at all times"
      },
      {
        "label": "E",
        "text": "The drug is distributed to only 1 compartment\noutside the vascular system"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "B",
    "explanation": "\"First-order\" means that the elimination rate is\nproportional to the concentration perfusing the\norgan of elimination. The half-life is a constant. The\nrate of elimination is proportional to the rate of\nadministration only at steady state. The order of\nelimination is independent of the number of\ncompartments into which a drug distributes.",
