    "explanation": "Phase 1 trials determine the probable limits of the\nsafe clinical dosage range in a small number of\nhealthy volunteers. In Phase 2, the drug is studied in\npatients with the target disease to determine its\nefficacy. In phase 3, the drug is evaluated in larger\nnumbers of patients with the target disease to\nfurther establish safety and efficacy. Phase 4\nconstitutes monitoring the safety of the new drug\nunder actual conditions of use in large number of\npatients. Katzung 10th ed., 70-71.",
